<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Sovereign Council of Asturias and León</h1><p class="st-meta">1937 CE – 1937 CE · capital Gijón</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Republican regional government in Asturias that declared itself sovereign when cut off from the rest of Republican Spain in 1937.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bilbao">Bilbao</a> fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-franco">Franco</a> in June 1937, and as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santander-spain">Santander</a> fell in late August, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a> and part of León were isolated from the Republican government in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>. On 24 August 1937 the Interprovincial Council at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gijon">Gijón</a>, led by the Socialist miners' leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarmino-tomas">Belarmino Tomás</a>, declared itself sovereign.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The council took over all civil and military powers, issued its own decrees and money, and tried to organise defence of the mountains and the mining valleys with exhausted troops and few supplies. The central government saw the declaration as a step too far, but could do little.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Nationalist forces broke through in October 1937. Leaders and soldiers fled by sea, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-franco">Franco</a>'s troops entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gijon">Gijón</a> on 21 October 1937, ending the war in the north.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sovereign-council-of-asturias-and-leon.jpg" alt="Sovereign Council of Asturias and León" width="320" height="171"><figcaption>Image: Emilio Gómez Fernández · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frente_del_Norte_-_Spanish_Civil_War_(March-Sept_1937).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1937 CE – 1937 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gijón</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Belarmino Tomás</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish, Asturian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Consejo Soberano de Asturias y León</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1937&amp;focus=sovereign-council-of-asturias-and-leon" aria-label="Sovereign Council of Asturias and León on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4543 634 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sovereign Council of Asturias and León lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4863 890L4909 989M4863 890L4909 989"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4909 989h0M4909 989h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4863 890h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4863 890h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Gijón. <a href="/atlas?year=1937&amp;focus=sovereign-council-of-asturias-and-leon">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
